# TP DECK agent constraints

Rules that the README and the release skill do not state.

- The GUI is PySide6. Bridge asyncio to Qt with `qasync`. Playwright uses its async API.
- The main panel is a floating tool window: `Qt.WindowType.WindowStaysOnTopHint | Qt.WindowType.Tool`.
- Persist the panel's screen position. On `closeEvent` and `moveEvent`, save `(X, Y)` to `settings.json` and restore it on startup, so the panel returns to the same monitor.
- When a run starts, disable that action. On the full panel, set its text to "⏳ Processing...". Leave the compact-strip button label alone. Re-enable the button in a `finally` block.
- Browser connections come from `settings.json`. Single uses port 9222. Dual uses eBay port 9222 and ERP port 9223. Do not hardcode them.
- Match a tab by the configured URL pattern. Call `document.hasFocus()` only when more than one tab matches.
- Run Playwright work inside an `asyncio.Task`. Emergency Stop and the Pause key must both call `task.cancel()` on that task immediately.
- Register Pause through the `keyboard` library. Do not hook the Windows keyboard API more broadly.
- Keep a rolling log at `tp_deck/tpdeck.log`.
